WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.915 --> 00:00:11.621
This page explains how the whole site works and how it sits beside Blackboard. The panel you are reading now appears on every page, always tuned to that page.

2
00:00:11.621 --> 00:00:20.286
Skim the cards in order. They cover Blackboard, privacy, copyright, translation, accessibility, and the site's known limits.

3
00:00:20.286 --> 00:00:31.292
Learn the loop with Blackboard. You learn and practise here; you submit, discuss, and get grades on Blackboard. If the two ever disagree, Blackboard is the source of truth.

4
00:00:31.292 --> 00:00:42.299
Open the Reading Lens when you need it. The button at the top of every page offers text size, spacing, a high-legibility font, page tints, a reading ruler, a magnifier, and read-aloud.

5
00:00:42.299 --> 00:00:53.311
Look for the How to use this page bar anywhere you go. Every page carries its own version of this panel with steps for that page. Open it whenever a page feels unfamiliar.

6
00:00:53.311 --> 00:01:02.909
Report anything broken. The Report a problem button opens your own email with the page details filled in. Nothing is collected by this site.

7
00:01:02.909 --> 00:01:13.911
On a shared computer, clear your work. The Clear my saved work button on this page removes everything this site has saved in this browser. Download your weekly notes first if you want to keep them.

8
00:01:13.915 --> 00:01:24.929
Back up your saved work. The Take your saved work with you box on this page downloads everything you have typed and rated as one file, and restores it on any device. The accessibility statement lives here too.

9
00:01:24.929 --> 00:01:30.493
Nothing on this site is graded. Blackboard is the only official gradebook.

10
00:01:30.494 --> 00:01:34.725
Where next: Head back Home and open the current week.
